    <node id="Paper_322">
      <data key="d0">Paper</data>
      <data key="d1">InfoVis</data>
      <data key="d2">2019</data>
      <data key="d3">There Is No Spoon: Evaluating Performance, Space Use, and Presence with Expert Domain Users in Immersive Analytics</data>
      <data key="d4">10.1109/tvcg.2019.2934803</data>
      <data key="d5">http://dx.doi.org/10.1109/TVCG.2019.2934803</data>
      <data key="d6">536.0</data>
      <data key="d7">546.0</data>
      <data key="d8">J</data>
      <data key="d9">Immersive analytics turns the very space surrounding the user into a canvas for data analysis, supporting human cognitive abilities in myriad ways. We present the results of a design study, contextual inquiry, and longitudinal evaluation involving professional economists using a Virtual Reality (VR) system for multidimensional visualization to explore actual economic data. Results from our preregistered evaluation highlight the varied use of space depending on context (exploration vs. presentation), the organization of space to support work, and the impact of immersion on navigation and orientation in the 3D analysis space.</data>
      <data key="d10">Andrea Batch;Andrew Cunningham;Maxime Cordeil;Niklas Elmqvist;Tim Dwyer;Bruce H. Thomas;Kim Marriott</data>
      <data key="d11">Andrea Batch;Andrew Cunningham;Maxime Cordeil;Niklas Elmqvist;Tim Dwyer;Bruce H. Thomas;Kim Marriott</data>
      <data key="d12">University of Maryland, College Park, USA;University of South Australia, Adelaide, Australia;Monash University, Melbourne, Australia;University of Maryland, College Park, USA;Monash University, Melbourne, Australia;University of South Australia, Adelaide, Australia;Monash University, Melbourne, Australia</data>
      <data key="d13">10.1109/tvcg.2017.2743990;10.1109/tvcg.2016.2599107;10.1109/visual.1990.146402;10.1109/tvcg.2012.219;10.1109/visual.1995.480800;10.1109/tvcg.2012.213;10.1109/tvcg.2018.2865191;10.1109/tvcg.2017.2743990</data>
      <data key="d14">Design study,evaluation,economic analysis,immersive analytics</data>
      <data key="d15">68.0</data>
      <data key="d16">82.0</data>
      <data key="d17">52.0</data>
      <data key="d18">2083.0</data>
      <data key="d19" />
      <data key="d20" />
